today's one minute monday is donate your  time i believe that as an entrepreneur  you have a responsibility to help the  people in the community and give back  and share your wisdom to make them  better so i was recently asked by  enactus to judge a student entrepreneur  competition for them the only problem  was it was on a monday i hate saying yes  to things on a monday i almost never do  it monday is my get stuff done for the  weekday it's where i get everything i  need done for the week so i can go enjoy  and have fun on the rest of the week but  it was an important cause and it was  helping entrepreneurs so i said yes it  took me basically the whole day there  listening to four entrepreneurs pitch  their ideas and giving them feedback to  help them pick a winner we finished  around four o'clock and i rushed to my  car to get back so i could start doing  work but on the car ride back all i  could think about was those four student  entrepreneurs and how their  presentations could have been better i  wish i had the opportunity to talk with  them and meet with them and give them  feedback on how they could improve for  the next time they go out and do it so  when i got back instead of going into  the work that i had missed for the  entire day i sat down and made four  videos for each of the entrepreneurs  giving them feedback i spent the next 40  minutes making individual videos for  them giving them personalized advice for  how they could improve i emailed them  the videos later that day and they were  all blown away with the advice and  feedback and i could tell that it really  made a difference for them so even  though i had work piling up and piling  up and piling up i spent the day to go  help them and then came back and made  those videos for them because it was the  right thing to do you have an obligation  and a duty to help others as well so  take some time this week to mentor  somebody and see the positive impact you  can have on their lives and believe 